% Background theory: pairwise distinctness, declared by the parties.
%
% DPV publishes nothing that separates these purposes.  The rule is
% the parties', on the ground that DPV defines each as a purpose in
% its own right, and a verdict resting on an instance of it is
% withdrawable by abandoning the rule.
%
% Distinctness, not disjointness: one purpose may lie below another
% and still be a different purpose.  Disjointness over a pair with a
% common child would contradict the resource, and this module
% publishes concepts below two parents.
%
% The rule is stated here and instantiated by the problems.  A
% problem naming two of the purposes below carries the inequation
% between them as a bg_dist_ assertion.
%
% Purposes: 4
% Pairs   : 6
%
% Advertising, Marketing, ResearchAndDevelopment, ScientificResearch
